R['fail-closed'][1] = """**CONFIRMED (C1-10), measured.** Current month partition `audit_events_y2026m10` detached at 21:08:07 (233 rows). (a) any audited mutation: `500 INTERNAL`, body `retryable: true`, text "An unexpected error occurred. Quote the request id when reporting it."; CLI exit code 5. A new login (`/login/passkey`) fails the same way (HTTP 500), so a person cannot sign in either; the bearer token of an already signed-in CLI still reads. (b) serve log: `{"level":"error","msg":"http.request_failed","causeCode":"control_store_query_failed","errorCode":"audit_append_failed","errorName":"AuditWriteError","requestId":"req_...","route":"/targets/{target}/migrations/plans"}` (the log carries the route template; the metric does not, see observability step 2). (c) `/healthz/ready` stayed 200 on serve, worker, gateway and public for the whole outage (sampled every second, no transition). (d) `GET /installation/health`: top state `operational`, all 8 components `operational`, no reason. (e) `observation.health_samples` kept growing (92 -> 120 in 100 s); the worker logged no warn/error. (f) `GET /api/v1/targets` 200. The four failed requests left no audit trace and no counter other than `exdb_http_requests_total{route="/unmatched",status_class="5xx"}`. Re-attached `ATTACH PARTITION ... FOR VALUES FROM ('2026-10-01') TO ('2026-11-01')` at 21:09:52: the next mutation succeeded at once, no restart, `audit verify` ok with 243 verified events. While detached, `max(seq)` through the parent is empty (the 233 existing rows are invisible), so any chain read in that state sees no history. Raw: `fc1.out`."""

R['fail-closed'][7] = """**CONFIRMED (C1-10, P3 stands).** With the partition detached (step 1) `POST /api/v1/targets/{dev18}/queries` with `select 's6mark...'` returned `500 INTERNAL` after 0.22 s, and the marker is in the target's statement log (`log_statement=all`, 1 hit): the SELECT ran on the target, the caller got an error and the read has no audit event. Raw: `fc1.out`."""

R['fail-closed'][2] = """**REFUTED as written (the injection does not make the store read-only for the product); a different, worse behaviour found.** `ALTER DATABASE exponetdb_control SET default_transaction_read_only = on` + terminating the 23 backends (21:10:25): **mutations kept succeeding** (plans created at t=2 s, 21 s, 64 s, 127 s; rows exist in `operations.plans`), because the Control Store opens write transactions with an explicit `BEGIN ... READ WRITE` (`packages/control-store/src/store.ts:158`), which overrides the database default. Single statements outside such a transaction (the heartbeat `UPDATE`, grant last-use) do fail with `25006` (`heartbeat.failed`, `oauth.grant_use_failed`, worker `dataread.tick_failed 25006` ~200/min, `maintenance.loop_failed`). Readiness: `/healthz/ready` 200 until t~32 s, then **503 on serve, worker and gateway** (`heartbeat_stale`, `workers no_live_worker`); `GET /installation/health` -> `down`. So the roles report not_ready (and in production serve would leave the proxy) while the worker's operations loop still writes. Recovery is not automatic: `ALTER DATABASE ... RESET` from a session of that database fails (`cannot execute ALTER DATABASE in a read-only transaction`: connect to `postgres`), and after the RESET (21:23:11) all three roles stayed 503 for 4 min 36 s because the pooled sessions kept the old default; only terminating the backends brought them back (ready 9 s later). New finding S6-2. See `fc2b` for the real read-only store (hot standby). Raw: `fc2.out`, `fc2-undo2.out`."""

R['fail-closed'][4] = """**PARTIAL: the first 14 s are 500 INTERNAL as C1 predicted, then it becomes 503 CONTROL_PLANE_DEGRADED (C1 said never).** `docker pause` of the Control Store 21:28:13, 60 s. t=3 s: mutation `500 INTERNAL` (took ~5 s, the pool connect timeout); t=8.6 s read `500` after 5.0 s. Readiness: serve, worker, gateway and public 503 from t=14.6 s. From then on every API call is answered immediately (1.8 ms) with `503 CONTROL_PLANE_DEGRADED` "ExponetDB itself is not ready. This says nothing about the target databases." (the gate of `api.ts:2184` applies whenever readiness is `not_ready`, not only for the catalog case). Logs: `control_store.pool_error` (9 per role), `heartbeat.failed` (`control_store_unavailable`, then `control_store_query_failed`), `http.request_failed ... control_store_unavailable`; gateway `agent.request INTERNAL` x5. Unpause at t=60.1: all roles ready again at t=63.5 (3.4 s), **no restart** (unit start times unchanged), first mutation after: success. In-flight apply (60 s `pg_sleep` migration on dev16, store paused 40 s, 12 s after the apply started): lease lost; events `lease_taken_over -> needs_reconciliation -> failed`; final `failed apply=not_applied`, ledger 0 rows, the first statement executed once (sequence = 1): no second execution, no half apply, resolved 11 s after unpause. The operator sees `failed / not_applied` and has to re-plan. Raw: `fc4.out`."""

R['fail-closed'][5] = """**CONFIRMED (C1-3), with numbers.** Baseline: 200 concurrent `GET /api/v1/targets` for 10 s = 4,002 requests, all 200, p50 496 ms, p99 701 ms. Then `LOCK TABLE registry.targets IN ACCESS EXCLUSIVE MODE` for 40 s (a stand-in for a slow store) with the same load for 55 s: 87,553 requests; 200: 6,389; **500 INTERNAL: 580** (571 `control_store_unavailable` = pool connect timeout reported as "unreachable" while the store is up, plus 10 `control_store_timeout` 57014 after the 30 s statement timeout); **503 CONTROL_PLANE_DEGRADED: 80,584** (fast failures after readiness flipped); max latency 30.5 s. Serve `/healthz/ready` went 503 at t=14.9 s (lock at t=4 s), flapped 200 at t=35 s, 503 again at 47 s, steadily 200 from t=52.7 s (8 s after the lock was released at t=44.3); worker and gateway stayed 200 (they were not loaded). A mutation at t=8.5 s: 500 INTERNAL. Recovery after release: first read 200 at t=45.9 s. In production the 503 on the Docker HEALTHCHECK would also drop serve from Traefik for the flapping period (not exercised: no Traefik on the stack). Raw: `fc5.out`."""

