R['fail-closed']['2b'] = """**CONFIRMED (C1-3), the real read-only store: a hot standby that was not promoted.** A `pg_basebackup -R` copy of the Control Store swapped in as the data directory (`pg_is_in_recovery() = t`). Mutations: `500 INTERNAL` (t=4.5 s and 17.4 s; `http.request_failed` with SQLSTATE `25006` and `0A000`, `heartbeat.failed control_store_query_failed`, `oauth.grant_use_failed 25006`); reads `200` for the first ~80 s; readiness 200 for ~35 s, then `/healthz/ready` 503 on serve, worker and gateway (`heartbeat_stale`, `workers no_live_worker`). Once not_ready every API call is `503 CONTROL_PLANE_DEGRADED` in ~1.5 ms (reads included). The CLI cannot refresh its access token on a read-only store: `oauth_server_error` ("The server refused the request (server_error)") and, after the token's 10 minutes, `401` on reads and on `/installation/health`. Promotion (`pg_ctl promote`): all three roles ready again 8.4 s later, no restart. Raw: `fc2b.out`."""

R['fail-closed'][3] = """**PARTIAL: confirmed worse than C1 expected: a full Control Store disk is not "writes fail, reads work" but a crash.** Data directory on a 420 MB loop-mounted ext4 (74 MB used). Filled through the unaudited bundle ingest (step 6): 5 requests (1 x 50 x 600 KB, then 8 x 3 MB each) took the free space from 296 MB to 12 MB; the 5th request answered `500 INTERNAL` and PostgreSQL logged `PANIC: could not write to file "pg_wal/xlogtemp.59": No space left on device` on a `COMMIT`, `server process terminated by signal 6`, crash recovery, `FATAL: could not write to file "pg_wal/xlogtemp.119"` during recovery and `shutting down due to startup process failure` **9 seconds after the first failed request**. The container exited and stays down (no restart policy in the stack; with `unless-stopped` it would loop in failing recovery). Serve, worker, gateway: `control_store.pool_error`, readiness 503 (`check_error` on control_store, role_credential, installation, schema, keyring, heartbeat), `ECONNREFUSED`. `VACUUM` / `audit prune`: `control_store_unavailable`. The rows cannot be removed to free space (append-only trigger, `DELETE refused`), so the only recovery is more disk. Recovery after growing the image (`truncate`, `losetup -c`, `resize2fs`): the filesystem grew; the stopped container had to be started by hand (not re-measured: the script reverted to the saved data directory). New finding S6-1. Raw: `fc3.out`."""

R['fail-closed'][6] = """**CONFIRMED (C1-11).** `POST /api/v1/projects/{id}/bundles` with the CLI token (scope `migrations.plan` only; the real path is `/projects/{id}/bundles`, not `.../migrations/bundles`): 50 distinct 600 KB bundles in one request: `200`, 1.2 s, `migrations.bundle_revisions` 3 -> 53 rows, 64 kB -> 31 MB; `max(seq)` of `audit.audit_events` before and after: 289 and 289 (no audit event for the ingest). `DELETE` as the superuser: `migrations.bundle_revisions is append-only (DELETE refused)`; as `exdb_serve`: `permission denied`. No rate limit: the next 4 requests (24 MB each) were accepted until the disk was full (step 3). Raw: `fc3.out`."""

